        "content": "<p>macovedj opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14460\">PR #14460</a> from <code>macovedj:component-async-coop-yield</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Wasmtime can keep processing ready, high-priority component work without yielding to the async executor. The two tests cover ways this can happen. In the first, a batch of spawned store tasks finishes before a sibling Tokio task gets a turn to send its oneshot result. In the second, cancellation callbacks repeatedly start and cancel new subtasks, keeping the event loop busy while a timer cannot complete.<br>\nThis change caps the number of event-loop work turns between yields at 128. I chose 128, inspired by <a href=\"https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/blob/tokio-1.51.1/tokio/src/task/coop/mod.rs#L105-L117\">Tokio’s cooperative budget</a>, but I’m happy to consider another cap or a different approach.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 628196311,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790801309
    },
